WHAT EACH ARCHITECTURE REACHES  (measured; no recommendation implied)
========================================================================

  What the weights are doing in this stage
  --------------------------------------------------------------------
    swapping the ordering key from combined risk to composite changes 29 of 100 recommendations (29%)

    The weights never order anything in this stage. They enter only
    through pool membership, and P15 above measures how much that
    boundary matters: read the figure printed there rather than any
    number quoted here, because it has moved.

    And the swap number is NOT evidence that the weights are
    decorative. The two keys agreeing means the choice is insensitive
    to which is used, and the reason is P13: one partner wins under
    both, so almost nothing is being ordered at all. Since coverage
    was removed from selection the winner changed but the
    concentration did not, which is section 6.5c: a partner scoring
    near zero in every organ minimises min(A,B) for every A, so any
    rule minimising combined risk picks it for everyone.

  Coverage and the escape population
  --------------------------------------------------------------------
    AND-gate coverage is the intersection. Escape is one minus it.
    Both are FLOORS: this is a single-nucleus assay and it drops
    transcripts, so the true intersection is higher and the true
    escape lower. The direction is known; the magnitude is not.

    Two coverage numbers, and both are needed. f_AB is the fraction
    itself; span %ile is where that fraction sits among measured pairs
    of similar gene length. Detection tracks span more strongly than it
    tracks expression, so a high f_AB on two long genes and a high one
    on two short genes do not mean the same thing. Neither number
    gates anything: coverage was removed from partner selection.

